CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Cost Analysis and Application\n-----------------------------\n\
 nIn  assignment 1\, your team made a presentation to the new board of Cap
 e Eco Furniture Co.\, focusing on the importance of managerial accounting 
 in enhancing cost management and operational efficiency. You were able to 
 analyse the company's current cost structure\, identified areas for optimi
 zation\, and demonstrated how managerial accounting practices could lead t
 o improved decision-making and profitability. The board was pleased with y
 our presentation and having realised issues with  allocating costs to the
  different product lines\, they have asked for your services again. See th
 e content below \n\nBackground Information\n----------------------\n\n* R
 evenue: Last year's total revenue: $5\,000\,000\n\n* Product Lines:\n\n* C
 ustom Furniture (Job Order Costing)\n\n* Standard Furniture (Process Costi
 ng)\n\n* Manufacturing Facility:\n\n* Location: Green City Industrial Park
   Cape town \n\n* Monthly Fixed Costs: $50\,000 (rent\, utilities\, sala
 ries)\n\n* Variable Costs: $100 per unit for standard items\, varying cost
 s for custom orders\n\n* Selling price :  $250 per unit for standard item
 s\, $300 for custom orders\n\nFinancial Data\n--------------\n\n* Standard
  Furniture Production (per month):\n\n* Units produced: 1\,000\n\n* Direct
  materials: $30\,000\n\n* Direct labor: $20\,000\n\n* Variable manufacturi
 ng overhead: $50\,000\n\n* Fixed manufacturing overhead: $30\,000\n\n* Cus
 tom Furniture Production (per month):\n\n* Average number of orders: 50\n\
 n* Direct materials: $1\,500 per order\n\n* Direct labor: $800 per order\n
 \n* Variable manufacturing overhead: $20\,000\n\n* Fixed manufacturing ove
 rhead: $20\,000\n\n* Selling and Administrative Expenses:\n\n* Fixed costs
 : $10\,000 per month\n\n* Variable costs: 5% of sales\n\nActivities on cos
 t Analysis and Application.\n--------------------------------------------\
 n\nCost Allocation:\n\n* Cape Eco Furniture Co.’s board has asked your t
 eam to come up with a presentation training junior managers how they  sho
 uld allocate the manufacturing overhead costs between standard and custom 
 furniture production.\n\n* Hint: Calculate the overhead allocation for eac
 h product line using an appropriate method (e.g.\, activity-based costing)
  and interpret your findings for better decision making. \n\nBreak-Even A
 nalysis:\n\n* The management needs to understand how the company is able t
 o make profits. In so doing\, you are tasked to make a presentation about 
 how to perform a break-even analysis for both product lines and make your 
 own interpretation about which product line is better for an informed deci
 sion making \n\n* Hint: Calculate the break-even point in units for stand
 ard furniture and the break-even point in orders for custom furniture then
  after compare and determine the better product for decision making.\n\nCo
 st Control Strategies:\n\n* The board for Cape Eco Furniture Co. also foun
 d out in the previous presentations that the company was incurring a lot o
 f costs both fixed and variable. As a team\, you have been employed to res
 earch and propose strategies that can be used by the company  to control 
 its variable and fixed costs without compromising its quality. \n\nScenar
 io Analysis:\n\n* Cape Eco Furniture Co has been advised to increase direc
 t material cost by 10% in order to increase productivity and profitability
 . The board is however not convinced with the reasons of the proposers. Th
 ey have therefore tasked you with analysing the impact of a 10% increase i
 n direct material costs on Cape Eco Furniture Co.’s profitability and pr
 oductivity \n\n* Hint: Recalculate the cost structure and determine the n
 ew break-even points for both product lines and then make a conclusion and
  a recommendation to the board. \n\nStrategic Decision-Making:\n\n* Based
  on the findings that you have made about cost analysis\, you are to make 
 a recommendation to the board on whether Cape Eco Furniture Co.. should fo
 cus more on custom furniture or standard furniture? Justify your answer wi
 th financial data.\n\nSubmission Type: PDF file\n\nSee  [Assignment Rubr
 ic Here] (https://docs.google.com/document/d/1byDBqAYN2mIY1v4wElCKsamvJN35
 -qDKe7jmsjqdxzQ/edit)\n\nClick 'Next' to access the week's quiz
