CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nThe Authentic Leadership Self-Assessment is a reflec
 tive tool that helps people evaluate their authentic leadership skills by 
 evaluating leadership across four key dimensions: self-awareness\, interna
 lized moral perspective\, balanced processing\, and relational transparenc
 y. This tool provides insights into your leadership strengths and areas fo
 r growth\, fostering greater alignment with your core values and enabling 
 you to develop trust\, ethical decision-making\, and effective leadership 
 practices.\n\nInstructions:\n\n* Complete the Authentic Leadership Self-As
 sessment questionnaire and upload it on canvas. [Download it here] (https:
 //alueducation.instructure.com/courses/2727/files/513675?wrap=1)\n\n* Read
  the chapter on Authentic Leadership available in Perusall to understand t
 he four dimensions in depth.\n\n* Respond to the following prompt and uplo
 ad your responses along with your Self-Assessment document:\n\nPrompt (1 P
 age Response)\n\n* Based on your assessment results and the chapter readin
 g\, reflect on the dimension in which you scored the highest and share wit
 h examples how this has served as a strength for you as an emerging leader
 . \n\n* Reflect on the dimension in which you scored the lowest\, how has
  this affected your effectiveness as an emerging leader? (share real examp
 les). 
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Week 5: Authentic Leadership Self-Assessment and Reflection [Africa
 _s_Leaders]
