DTSTART;VALUE=DATE;VALUE=DATE:20260726
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Individual Mission Project\n\n \n\nSummative Instructions\n\nY
 ou are coming to the end of your Creativity and Innovation course. You hav
 e grappled with stakeholder analysis\, experimentation\, root cause analys
 is and problem framing to look at your mission in new and creative ways. Y
 ou have also learned about the importance of storytelling to help you comm
 unicate your innovative ideas in compelling ways.\n\nIf you've engaged wit
 h this process correctly\, the frame of your mission or the lens through w
 hich you look at it should have changed (even if only slightly). You will 
 have also become better at telling stories about your mission.\n\nWith thi
 s in mind\, your submission should speak to the following:\n\n*\n\nWhat is
  your (updated) mission-related challenge or opportunity? Capture this in 
 a 50-75 word mission statement or description.\n\n*\n\nUsing the Story Spi
 ne concept as a guide\, write a short paragraph that tells a story about y
 our mission\, a protagonist and proposed solution. This should be no more 
 than 250 words.\n\n* A short reflection on where you see your mission proj
 ect going. Think about any insights you gained\, mistakes\, surprises and 
 lessons learned throughout the course. This should be no more than 150 wor
 ds.\n\n*\n\nSubmit your work as a single PDF or Word Doc. No other file ty
 pe will be accepted.\n\n* Remember to include a signed plagiarism declarat
 ion/statement of academic integrity with your submission.\n\n \n\nTips on
  character development:\n\n* Like any great story\, your story will need a
  protagonist. Once you have developed your story spine\, spend some time o
 n character development. Identify the main characters in the story (e.g. t
 he customer\, the business owner)\, and describe them in detail. What are 
 their motivations? What challenges do they face? What are their goals? Con
 sider the challenges that the characters face and how they overcome them (
 using your business idea).\n\n* And yes\, you can be the protagonist 🙂\
 n\n \n\n \n\n 
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Week 8 Individual Summative: Mission Statement and Storytelling [Cr
 eativity_and_Innovation]
