UID:event-assignment-41511
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE;VALUE=DATE:20260728
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Case study: Building a Responsible Food System in Pastoral Comm
 unities in Rural Africa\n-------------------------------------------------
 -------------------------------------\n\nIn many African communities\, esp
 ecially pastoralist communities rely heavily on livestock (especially catt
 le\, goats\, and camels) for their economic livelihoods\, cultural identit
 y\, and food security. However\, climate change\, land degradation\, popul
 ation pressures\, and shifting consumption patterns are threatening the su
 stainability of these traditional systems.\n\nRecurring droughts have led 
 to massive livestock losses. Meanwhile\, younger generations are moving to
  cities or showing less interest in traditional herding. Livestock product
 ion also contributes to methane emissions\, raising questions about enviro
 nmental sustainability. At the same time\, there is rising demand for meat
  and dairy in urban areas\, and companies are starting to explore commerci
 al ventures to “modernize” the sector.\n\nThe challenge is now to desi
 gn a responsible\, inclusive\, and climate-smart livestock economy that:\n
 \n* Respects cultural traditions\,\n\n* Empowers pastoralist communities (
 especially women and youth)\,\n\n* Protects the environment\, and\n\n* Cre
 ates value through innovation and enterprise.\n\n--------------\nInstructi
 ons: \n--------------\n\nYour Task:\n\nPick a rural community in Africa\,
  facing these issues - make sure to pick one that you can do in-depth rese
 arch on\n(For e.g - The Masai of Kenya and Tanzania\, The Fulani group in 
 Western Africa and the Banyamulenge in Eastern DRC etc. )\n\nDesign a 12-y
 ear plan to build a responsible enterprise around sustainable livestock an
 d food systems in the chosen rural community. Your plan should:\n\n* Pleas
 e provide a background/context about the chosen rural community in Africa.
  This should include the geographical\, economical\, social\, and historic
 al context. \n\n* Craft a clear problem statement.\n\n* Use 4 future arch
 etypes to describe how this sector could evolve\, where possible use avail
 able data/trends to describe the below:\n\n* Expected future\n\n* Worse th
 an expected\n\n* Better than expected\n\n* Weirder than expected\n\n* Base
 d on the "Better Than Expected" future\, propose 3 human-centered enterpri
 se ideas\, here is a quick example (come up with a different one in your p
 resentation):\n\n* Community-owned dairy cooperatives using solar-powered 
 cooling\n\n* Evaluate your solutions using the below criteria:\n\n* Circul
 ar economy principles (e.g.\, biogas from waste\, zero-waste dairy product
 ion)\n\n* Inclusion of marginalized groups (e.g.\, women herders\, nomadic
  youth)\n\n* CSR principles: ethical sourcing\, animal welfare\, local emp
 owerment\n\n* Choose a final/best  solution based on the criteria and dem
 onstrate how those criteria are being fulfilled. \n\n* Develop a 12-year 
 roadmap using the 3-Horizon Framework demonstrating which and when milesto
 nes will be achieved\;\n\n* Horizon 1: The way things are\, the current sy
 stem as it is(0-3 years). \n\n* Horizon 2: How things could be in the sho
 rt-term\, innovations which\, if developed\, could help bring out a differ
 ent system(3-5 years). \n\n* Horizon 3: The desired future system which c
 ould come about with consistent positive progress(5-12 years)\n\n8. For yo
 ur chosen solution\, provide:\n                  - Stakeholder An
 alysis\n                  - Cost Analysis\n              
     - Solution limitations and major challenges\n\n---------------------
 -----------------\nKindly note the submission guidelines:\n---------------
 -----------------------\n\n-------------------\nPresentation Format\n-----
 --------------\n\n* Maximum of 15 slides\n\n* Slides should be visually ap
 pealing and professionally designed\n\n* Use relevant visuals\, charts\, a
 nd graphics where appropriate\n\n-----------------------\nFormatting Requi
 rements\n-----------------------\n\n* Font Type: Montserrat\n\n* Font Size
  and Color: Consistent and easily readable throughout\n\n* Referencing Sty
 le: APA 7th Edition\n\n-------------------------------\nVideo Presentation
  Requirements\n-------------------------------\n\nIn addition to your slid
 e deck\, you are required to record an individual presentation of your wor
 k.\n\nYour video must meet the following requirements:\n\n* Maximum length
 : 7 minutes\n\n* You must present your slides yourself\n\n* Your face must
  be clearly visible throughout the presentation\n\n* Dress in professional
  attire\n\n* Record in a quiet\, professional\, and distraction-free envir
 onment\n\n* Ensure your audio is clear and audible\n\n* Demonstrate famili
 arity with your work rather than reading directly from the slides\n\nPleas
 e note that presentation quality\, professionalism\, and clarity of commun
 ication will form part of the assessment.\n\n-----------------------\nSubm
 ission Deliverables\n-----------------------\n\n* PowerPoint/PDF slide dec
 k with a link to your video recording of your presentation (7 minutes maxi
 mum)\n\n \n\n 
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Summative:  [Responsible_Enterprise]
