X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<h3><span style="font-size: 14pt\;"><span>Case
  study</span><i><span>: </span></i><strong><i>Building a Responsible Food 
 System in Pastoral Communities in Rural Africa</i></strong></span></h3>\n<
 p><span>In many African communities\, especially pastoralist communities r
 ely heavily on livestock (especially cattle\, goats\, and camels) for thei
 r economic livelihoods\, cultural identity\, and food security. However\, 
 climate change\, land degradation\, population pressures\, and shifting co
 nsumption patterns are threatening the sustainability of these traditional
  systems.</span></p>\n<p><span>Recurring droughts have led to massive live
 stock losses. Meanwhile\, younger generations are moving to cities or show
 ing less interest in traditional herding. Livestock production also contri
 butes to methane emissions\, raising questions about environmental sustain
 ability. At the same time\, there is rising demand for meat and dairy in u
 rban areas\, and companies are starting to explore commercial ventures to 
 “modernize” the sector.</span></p>\n<p><span>The challenge is now to d
 esign a responsible\, inclusive\, and climate-smart livestock economy that
 :</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li aria-level="1"><span>Respects cultural traditions\
 ,</span></li>\n<li aria-level="1"><span>Empowers pastoralist communities (
 especially women and youth)\,</span></li>\n<li aria-level="1"><span>Protec
 ts the environment\, and</span></li>\n<li aria-level="1"><span>Creates val
 ue through innovation and enterprise.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2><em><strong>
 Instructions:&nbsp\;</strong></em></h2>\n<p><span>Your Task:</span></p>\n<
 p><span>Pick a rural community in Africa\, facing these issues - make sure
  to pick one that you can do in-depth research on</span><span><br></span><
 span>(For e.g - The Masai of Kenya and Tanzania\, The Fulani group in West
 ern Africa and the Banyamulenge in Eastern DRC etc. )</span><span><br></sp
 an><span><br></span><span>Design a 12-year plan to build a responsible ent
 erprise around sustainable livestock and food systems in the chosen rural 
 community. Your plan should:</span></p>\n<ol>\n<li aria-level="1"><span>Pl
 ease provide a background/context about the chosen rural community in Afri
 ca. This should include the geographical\, economical\, social\, and histo
 rical context.&nbsp\;</span></li>\n<li aria-level="1"><span>Craft a clear 
 problem statement.</span></li>\n<li aria-level="1"><span>Use 4 future arch
 etypes to describe how this sector could evolve\, where possible use avail
 able data/trends to describe the below:</span><span><br><br></span></li>\n
 <ul>\n<li aria-level="2"><span>Expected future</span></li>\n<li aria-level
 ="2"><span>Worse than expected</span></li>\n<li aria-level="2"><span>Bette
 r than expected</span></li>\n<li aria-level="2"><span>Weirder than expecte
 d</span><span><br><br></span></li>\n</ul>\n<li aria-level="1"><span>Based 
 on the "Better Than Expected" future\, propose 3 human-centered enterprise
  ideas\, here is a quick example (come up with a different one in your pre
 sentation):</span><span><br><br></span></li>\n<ul>\n<li aria-level="2"><sp
 an>Community-owned dairy cooperatives using solar-powered cooling</span><s
 pan><br><br></span></li>\n</ul>\n<li aria-level="1"><span>Evaluate your so
 lutions using the below criteria:</span><span><br><br></span></li>\n<ul>\n
 <li aria-level="2"><span>Circular economy principles (e.g.\, biogas from w
 aste\, zero-waste dairy production)</span></li>\n<li aria-level="2"><span>
 Inclusion of marginalized groups (e.g.\, women herders\, nomadic youth)</s
 pan></li>\n<li aria-level="2"><span>CSR principles: ethical sourcing\, ani
 mal welfare\, local empowerment</span><span><br><br></span></li>\n</ul>\n<
 li aria-level="1"><span>Choose a final/best&nbsp\; solution based on the c
 riteria and demonstrate how those criteria are being fulfilled.&nbsp\;</sp
 an></li>\n<li aria-level="1"><span>Develop a 12-year roadmap using the 3-H
 orizon Framework demonstrating which and when milestones will be achieved\
 ;</span></li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li aria-level="1"><span>Horizon 1: The way th
 ings are\, the current system as it is(0-3 years).&nbsp\;</span></li>\n<li
  aria-level="1"><span>Horizon 2: How things could be in the short-term\, i
 nnovations which\, if developed\, could help bring out a different system(
 3-5 years).&nbsp\;</span></li>\n<li aria-level="1"><span>Horizon 3: The de
 sired future system which could come about with consistent positive progre
 ss(5-12 years)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span>8. For your chosen solution\, 
 provide:</span><span><br></span><span>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbs
 p\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; - Stakeholder Analysis</span><span><br
 ></span><span>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbs
 p\; &nbsp\; - Cost Analysis</span><span><br></span><span>&nbsp\; &nbsp\; &
 nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; &nbsp\; - Solution limitati
 ons and major challenges</span></p>\n<h2><strong><em>Kindly note the submi
 ssion guidelines:</em></strong></h2>\n<h2><em>Presentation Format</em></h2
 >\n<ul data-spread="false">\n<li><span>Maximum of 15 slides</span></li>\n<
 li><span>Slides should be visually appealing and professionally designed</
 span></li>\n<li><span>Use relevant visuals\, charts\, and graphics where a
 ppropriate</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2><span style="color: #e62429\;"><em>Form
 atting Requirements</em></span></h2>\n<ul data-spread="false">\n<li><span>
 Font Type: Montserrat</span></li>\n<li><span>Font Size and Color: Consiste
 nt and easily readable throughout</span></li>\n<li><span>Referencing Style
 : APA 7th Edition</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2><em><span style="color: #e62429\
 ;">Video Presentation Requirements</span></em></h2>\n<p class="isSelectedE
 nd"><span>In addition to your slide deck\, you are required to record an i
 ndividual presentation of your work.</span></p>\n<p class="isSelectedEnd">
 <span>Your video must meet the following requirements:</span></p>\n<ul dat
 a-spread="false">\n<li><span>Maximum length: 7 </span><strong><span>minute
 s</span></strong></li>\n<li><span>You must present your slides yourself</s
 pan></li>\n<li><span>Your face must be clearly visible throughout the pres
 entation</span></li>\n<li><span>Dress in professional attire</span></li>\n
 <li><span>Record in a quiet\, professional\, and distraction-free environm
 ent</span></li>\n<li><span>Ensure your audio is clear and audible</span></
 li>\n<li><span>Demonstrate familiarity with your work rather than reading 
 directly from the slides</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p class="isSelectedEnd"><spa
 n>Please note that presentation quality\, professionalism\, and clarity of
  communication will form part of the assessment.</span></p>\n<h2><em><stro
 ng>Submission Deliverables</strong></em></h2>\n<ol start="1" data-spread="
 false">\n<li><strong><span style="color: #000000\;"><em>PowerPoint/PDF sli
 de deck with a link to your video recording of your presentation (7 minute
 s maximum)</em></span></strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p>&nbsp\;</p>\n<p>&nbsp\;</p
 >
END:VEVENT
