DESCRIPTION:WEEK 4: Research Paper\n\nIn this assignment\, you will researc
 h the health problem you are addressing in your mission. Formulate an argu
 ment regarding the cause of this problem or a proposed solution. Support a
 nd substantiate your arguments with reputable scholarly research and popul
 ar press sources\, ensuring all are correctly and comprehensively cited.\n
 \nYour introductory paragraph should provide a brief overview of the probl
 em and include a compelling thesis statement. Interpret the findings in re
 lation to the research question or hypothesis\, and propose areas for furt
 her investigation based on these findings.\n\n \n\nIn this assignment\, y
 ou will investigate the health problem you are focusing on in your mission
 . Follow these steps to complete your research paper:\n\n* Research the He
 alth Problem:\n\n* Identify the Issue: Clearly define the health problem 
 you are addressing. Provide background information to give context to your
  research.\n\n* Gather Evidence: Use reputable sources\, including schola
 rly articles and popular press\, to gather information about the health pr
 oblem. Ensure that all sources are credible and relevant.\n\n* Formulate a
 n Argument:\n\n* Develop a thesis: Based on your research\, formulate a c
 lear and compelling argument. Decide whether you want to argue about the c
 ause of the health problem or propose a solution.\n\n* Support Your Argume
 nt: Use evidence from your research to support your argument. Make sure t
 o include data\, facts\, and examples that reinforce your position.\n\n* C
 ite Your Sources:\n\n* Proper Citations: Accurately and comprehensively c
 ite all the sources you use in your paper. USE APA citation style for both
  scholarly research and popular press sources.\n\n* Write Your Paper:\n\n*
  Introduction: Start with a brief overview of the health problem. Clearly
  state your thesis\, which is the main argument or point of your paper.\n\
 n* Discussion: In the body of your paper\, interpret your findings in rel
 ation to the research question or hypothesis. Discuss how your evidence su
 pports your argument.\n\n* Propose Future Research: Based on your finding
 s\, suggest areas where further research is needed. Explain why these area
 s are important and how they could contribute to solving the health proble
 m.\n\n* Conclusion:\n\n* Summarize Key Points: Recap the main findings of
  your research and how they support your argument.\n\n* Restate Thesis: R
 eiterate your thesis in light of the evidence presented.\n\n  6. Recommen
 dations: Offer recommendations or insights based on your analysis and sug
 gest practical steps for addressing the health problem.\n\nNotes: \n\n* B
 e sure to include at least five reliable sources (the sources have to be
  among the following: peer-reviewed articles\, official documents from gov
 ernments or relevant organizations). Also cite all the sources of informat
 ion used in your work. Follow APA 7 citation style.\n\n* You can use other
  sources as an addition to support the required items if they are relevant
  to your topic.\n\n* You can use AI tools to brainstorm\, but do not cop
 y-paste AI-generated answers as your own. If you happen to use AI\, inclu
 de an annex section after the reference list showing all the prompts and 
 outputs you used in your brainstorming.\n\n* Using Generative AI tools and
  not recognizing it will be considered as academic misconduct.\n\nSubmissi
 on:\n\nSubmit a PDF document. Links to Google Docs won't be accepted.
